ntly, it is set to use `http://localhost:3000` by default . 2. On the signin page, enter `admin` for username and password . 3. Click **Sign in**.'}, {'title': 'Manage user preferences | Grafana documentation', 'href': 'https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/latest/administration/user-management/user-preferences/', 'body': 'Grafana allows you to manage certain aspects of your user account, including your user name , email, and password . You can also view important information about your account, such as the organizations and roles to which you are assigned and the Grafana sessions associated with your account.'}, {'title': 'Common Issues with Grafana Login and How to Fix Them | Last9', 'href': 'https://last9.io/blog/grafana-login/', 'body': 'This guide covers the frequent login problems you might face and walks you through practical ways to resolve them. The Default Grafana Username and Password .This is the default setup — Grafana keeps usernames and passwords in its database.'}, {'title': 'Essential Grafana User Authentication Setup Methods - HostFoundry', 'href': 'https://declared.hostingpost.com/', 'body': 'Setting up user authentication in Grafana involves choosing from multiple methods like Basic, OAuth, LDAP, or SAML to secure your dashboards and data. For self-hosted instances, configuration is primarily handled by editing the grafana .ini file.'}, {'title': 'Learn how to configure Grafana and understand configuration options.', 'href': 'https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/latest/setup-grafana/configure-grafana/', 'body': 'The password of the default Grafana Admin. Set once on first-run. Sets the total stats collector interval. The default is 1800 seconds (30 minutes). basic_auth_ username and basic_auth_ password .'}]
