ed."}, {'title': 'Setting Up Joplin with Docker Compose - Techdox Docs', 'href': 'https://docs.techdox.nz/joplin/', 'body': "logo. Techdox Docs. Setting Up Joplin with Docker Compose. Password : admin. These are the default login credentials for Joplin Server upon the first run. It's strongly recommended to change these credentials after your initial login to ensure the security of your instance."}, {'title': 'Joplin default username / password - TechOverflow', 'href': 'https://techoverflow.net/2023/05/22/joplin-default-username-password/', 'body': 'May 22, 2023 · The default credentials for the Joplin note app are: Username : admin@localhost Password : admin Source: Server README on Github'}, {'title': 'Joplin Server Documentation - Features - Joplin Forum', 'href': 'https://discourse.joplinapp.org/t/joplin-server-documentation/24026', 'body': "Feb 26, 2022 · By default , Joplin Server will be setup with an admin user with email admin@localhost and password admin. For security purposes, the admin user's credentials should be changed."}, {'title': 'Joplin | MindlessTux', 'href': 'https://mindlesstux.com/2023/09/19/Joplin/', 'body': 'Sep 19, 2023 · By default , Joplin Server will be setup with an admin user with email admin@localhost and password admin. For security purposes, the admin user’s credentials should be changed. On the Admin Page, login as the admin user. In the upper right, select the Profile button update the admin password .'}, {'title': 'joplin/server - Docker Image', 'href': 'https://hub.docker.com/r/joplin/server', 'body': "By default , Joplin Server will be setup with an admin user with email admin@localhost and password admin. For security purposes, the admin user's credentials should be changed."}, {'title': 'Host Your Own Joplin Server with Docker on Ubuntu Guide | Vultr Docs', 'href': 'https://docs.vultr.com/how-to-host-a-joplin-server-with-docker-on-ubuntu', 'body': 'Log in to the Joplin server with the following default email and password .Click your username , Admin, in the top right corner. Edit your Administrator profile by filling in the Full name , Email, and Password fields.'}, {'title': 'Setting up your own Joplin Server note taking solution on... | Medium', 'href': 'https://leduccc.medium.com/setting-up-your-own-joplin-server-note-taking-solution-on-docker-with-portainer-9bc955dcb2dd', 'body': 'By default , Joplin Server will be set up with an admin user using the email admin@localhost and password admin. Change your password and confirm your email. You are now ready to configure synchronization for all your devices!'}, {'title': 'Self-host your notes: How to set up a private Joplin server the easy way', 'href': 'https://www.groovypost.com/howto/self-host-private-joplin-server/', 'body': 'To set up your own Joplin server , you’ll need a computer or other device to host the server . This needs to be a device that is always on, since if the host is turned off, you won’t be able to sync your Joplin notes. There are plenty of options available.'}, {'title': 'How to Self-Host Joplin Server with Docker | selfhosting.sh', 'href': 'https://selfhosting.sh/apps/joplin-server/', 'body': 'By default , Joplin Server limits upload size. Set MAX_ASSET_SIZE in bytes to increase: environment: MAX_ASSET_SIZE: 209715200 # 200 MB. Set up a reverse proxy to access Joplin Server over HTTPS. Point your proxy to port 22300.'}]
