[2026-08-03 06:29:05,543][scanner.cred_searcher][DEBUG] cred search web queries found these results: [{'title': 'Passwordcockpit is a simple, free, open source, self hosted, web...', 'href': 'https://passwordcockpit.com/', 'body': "Admin password to log into passwordcockpit . Passwordcockpit _upload_accepted_mimetypes. Specify accepted mime types to check when uploading a file, default value 'pdf'."}, {'title': 'Cockpit Authentication', 'href': 'https://cockpit-project.org/guide/latest/authentication', 'body': 'Cockpit Authentication. Table of Contents. Directly logging into the primary server.This can be done if you have direct network access to port 9090 on that server. By default the cockpit web service is installed on the base system and socket activated by systemd.'}, {'title': 'Passwordcockpit — unsubbed.co', 'href': 'https://unsubbed.co/tools/passwordcockpit/', 'body': 'Passwordcockpit is a self-hosted, web-based password manager built for teams. It is made in PHP, JavaScript, and MySQL or MariaDB, runs as a Docker service, and lets users store, share, and retrieve passwords , certificates, and file attachments from any device [README].'}, {'title': 'How to Manage Linux Servers with the Cockpit Web Interface', 'href': 'https://www.howtogeek.com/702841/how-to-manage-linux-servers-with-the-cockpit-web-interface/', 'body': 'sudo systemctl start cockpit in a terminal window. When Cockpit launches, the login screen appears; just log in with your existing Linux credentials . To connect to other computers using these same credentials , select the checkbox next to "Reuse My Password for Remote Connections."'}, {'title': 'Not able to login to cockpit using default credentials as user is locked', 'href': 'https://forum.camunda.io/t/not-able-to-login-to-cockpit-using-default-credentials-as-user-is-locked/28428', 'body': 'Hi @teja_polisetty, You can access it through the URL http://localhost:8088/h2/h2 Then use sa as password .'}, {'title': '11 Free and Open-source Password Alternatives and 1 password ...', 'href': 'https://medevel.com/1password-alternatives-1100/', 'body': '5- Password cockpit . Password cockpit is a simple, free, open source, self hosted, web based password manager for teams. It is made in PHP, Javascript, MySQL or MariaDB and it run on a docker service.'}, {'title': 'passwordcockpit / passwordcockpit - Docker Image', 'href': 'https://hub.docker.com/r/passwordcockpit/passwordcockpit/tags', 'body': 'Passwordcockpit is a simple, free, open source, self hosted, web based password manager for teams.docker pull passwordcockpit / passwordcockpit :1.4.0. Copy. Digest.'}, {'title': 'Log in to the Cockpit Web Console', 'href': 'https://docs.oracle.com/en/operating-systems/oracle-linux/cockpit/cockpit-install_logging_into_cockpit.html', 'body': 'In the Cockpit Login page, enter the system username and password . The image displays the Cockpit Login dialog, which shows the fields for Username and Password , and a field for Other options that you can optionally use to connect to a remote host.'}, {'title': 'Cockpit | Proxmox VE Scripts', 'href': 'https://proxmox-scripts.com/posts/cockpit/', 'body': '/etc/ cockpit / cockpit .conf. Notes. Set a root password if using autologin. This will be the Cockpit password . To set root password run sudo passwd root. If you plan on using 45Drives extension with NFS, you must setup LXC as privileged.'}, {'title': "Kali's Default Credentials | Kali Linux Documentation", 'href': 'https://www.kali.org/docs/introduction/default-credentials/', 'body': 'Password : . Default Tool Credentials . Some tools shipped with Kali, will use their own default hardcoded credentials (others will generate a new password the first time its used). The following tools have the default values'}, {'title': 'Passwordcockpit', 'href': 'https://passwordcockpit.com/', 'body': 'When the service is up, navigate to PASSWORDCOCKPIT _BASEHOST (e.g. https:// passwordcockpit .com) and login . The default username is admin. The system generate the default password : Admin123!, this can be overridden by specifying the PASSWORDCOCKPIT_ADMIN_ PASSWORD variable.'}, {'title': 'passwordcockpit/README.md at master · passwordcockpit ...', 'href': 'https://github.com/passwordcockpit/passwordcockpit/blob/master/README.md', 'body': 'The default username is admin. The system generate the default password : Admin123!, this can be overridden by specifying the PASSWORDCOCKPIT _ADMIN_ PASSWORD variable.'}, {'title': 'GitHub - passwordcockpit/passwordcockpit: Passwordcockpit is ... Cockpit Authentication The PasswordCockpit Open Source Project on Open Hub Default admin & admin user/pass do not work for login ... Setting user password', 'href': 'https://github.com/passwordcockpit/passwordcockpit', 'body': 'Passwordcockpit is a simple, free, open source, self hosted, web based password manager for teams. It is made in PHP, Javascript, MySQL or MariaDB and it run on a docker service. It allows users with any kind of device to safely store, share and retrieve passwords, certificates, files and much more. See full list on github.com See full list on github.com Installation is done with docker-compose. Please check out the official install instructions for more information. Passwordcockpit docker images are provided within its Docker Hub organization. To start, just copy docker-compose.yml to a folder and setup the configuration as shown in the "Available docker configurations" chapter. Finally run docker-compose up from terminal. When the service is up, navigate to PASSWORDCOCKPIT_BASEHOST (e.g. https:// passwordcockpit .com) and login . See full list on github.com Each user can have following permissions: ⚫️ Nothing (a normal user) 👥 Create and manage users 📁 Create folders 🗄 Access to all directories 📊 Can view log See full list on github.com Each folder has a list of associated users with their permissions: ⛔️ No access (A user cannot access a folder to which is not assigned) 👁 Read (A user can read the passwords from a folder to which he is associated) ✏️ Manage (The user can add, modify and delete passwords inside the folder) See full list on github.com Authentication can be done with database stored password or LDAP. See full list on github.com To use LDAP, users must exist in Passwordcockpit . The match of PASSWORDCOCKPIT_LDAP_ACCOUNTFILTERFORMAT is done with the username. When LDAP is enabled it is no longer possible to modify the profile data, since they will be synchronized at each login . See full list on github.com There are 3 levels of encryption: • Password PIN •SSL encryption for transfering data to the server •Database encryption for login informations, passwords and files. See full list on github.com A password can be crypted with a personal PIN in order to hide it from users with "Access to all directiories" permission and from users assigned to the same directory. See full list on github.com Password cockpit is translated into: •English •Italiano •Français See full list on github.com 3 days ago · By default this is configured to allow you to login with the username and password of any local account on the system. You can also setup a Kerberos based SSO solution or certificate/smart card authentication. Passwordcockpit is a simple, free, open source, self hosted, web based password manager for teams. It is made in PHP, Javascript, MySQL and it run on a docker service. Jun 8, 2024 · I am wanting to test drive the software but I am not able to login to the admin backend to change the password and username. Did I do something wrong or is this a botched installation ?. The Control Cockpit user interface is protected by SSL encryption by default . When you start the application for the first time, you will be prompted to enter a password for the user interface. What is passwordcockpit? Passwordcockpit is a simple, free, open source, self hosted, web based password manager for teams . It is made in PHP, Javascript, MySQL or MariaDB and it run on a docker service. It allows users with any kind of device to safely store, share and retrieve passwords, certificates, files and much more. Installation is done with docker-compose. What is the default password? The default username is admin. The system generate the default password: Admin123 !, this can be overridden by specifying the PASSWORDCOCKPIT_ADMIN_PASSWORD variable. Users can be associated to a folder even if they do not have permission from the parent folder. Authentication can be done with database stored password or LDAP. How to use LDAP in passwordcockpit? To use LDAP, users must exist in Passwordcockpit . The match of PASSWORDCOCKPIT_LDAP_ACCOUNTFILTERFORMAT is done with the username. When LDAP is enabled it is no longer possible to modify the profile data, since they will be synchronized at each login. There are 3 levels of encryption: Database encryption for login informations, passwords and files. How do I install passwordcockpit Docker? Installation is done with docker-compose . Please check out the official install instructions for more information. Passwordcockpit docker images are provided within its Docker Hub organization. To start, just copy docker-compose.yml to a folder and setup the configuration as shown in the "Available docker configurations" chapter.'}, {'title': 'The PasswordCockpit Open Source Project on Open Hub Default admin & admin user/pass do not work for login ... Setting user password', 'href': 'https://openhub.net/p/PasswordCockpit', 'body': 'Passwordcockpit is a simple, free, open source, self hosted, web based password manager for teams. It is made in PHP, Javascript, MySQL and it run on a docker service. Jun 8, 2024 · I am wanting to test drive the software but I am not able to login to the admin backend to change the password and username. Did I do something wrong or is this a botched installation ?. The Control Cockpit user interface is protected by SSL encryption by default . When you start the application for the first time, you will be prompted to enter a password for the user interface. What is passwordcockpit? Passwordcockpit is a simple, free, open source, self hosted, web based password manager for teams . It is made in PHP, Javascript, MySQL or MariaDB and it run on a docker service. It allows users with any kind of device to safely store, share and retrieve passwords, certificates, files and much more. Installation is done with docker-compose. What is the default password? The default username is admin. The system generate the default password: Admin123 !, this can be overridden by specifying the PASSWORDCOCKPIT_ADMIN_PASSWORD variable. Users can be associated to a folder even if they do not have permission from the parent folder. Authentication can be done with database stored password or LDAP. How to use LDAP in passwordcockpit? To use LDAP, users must exist in Passwordcockpit . The match of PASSWORDCOCKPIT_LDAP_ACCOUNTFILTERFORMAT is done with the username. When LDAP is enabled it is no longer possible to modify the profile data, since they will be synchronized at each login. There are 3 levels of encryption: Database encryption for login informations, passwords and files. How do I install passwordcockpit Docker? Installation is done with docker-compose . Please check out the official install instructions for more information. Passwordcockpit docker images are provided within its Docker Hub organization. To start, just copy docker-compose.yml to a folder and setup the configuration as shown in the "Available docker configurations" chapter.'}, {'title': 'Default admin & admin user/pass do not work for login ...', 'href': 'https://discourse.getcockpit.com/t/default-admin-admin-user-pass-do-not-work-for-login/2980', 'body': 'Jun 8, 2024 · I am wanting to test drive the software but I am not able to login to the admin backend to change the password and username. Did I do something wrong or is this a botched installation ?.'}, {'title': 'Setting user password', 'href': 'https://docs.cloud.sennheiser.com/en-us/control-cockpit/control-cockpit/setting-user-pw.html', 'body': 'The Control Cockpit user interface is protected by SSL encryption by default . When you start the application for the first time, you will be prompted to enter a password for the user interface.'}, {'title': 'Passwordcockpit — unsubbed.co', 'href': 'https://unsubbed.co/tools/passwordcockpit/', 'body': 'Database-stored passwords ( default ). LDAP with configurable account filter format; profile data syncs from LDAP on each login when LDAP mode is active [README].'}, {'title': 'Default Router Settings - Router Network', 'href': 'https://router-network.com/', 'body': 'Router Login . Default IP Addresses.To configure your router you must log in to it and know its IP address.'}, {'title': 'Ubiquiti Default Password - Compilation of Working Passwords', 'href': 'https://theinfocentric.com/ubiquiti-default-password/', 'body': 'We have gathered all working passwords for Ubiquiti Default Password for your comfort in the post.Enter the key or select the login button. If you encounter a login error, try retrieving your router’s default login credentials and attempting again.'}, {'title': 'Note that there are different passwords when logging in to the device.', 'href': 'https://revolutionpi.com/en/knowledge/device-password', 'body': 'The Default Password .When you log in for the first time, you are asked to create your own password . You can use Cockpit to change the password for the user pi or create additional accounts.'}]
